          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 12.123,
          "en": "as you learned, but what exactly is this code doing here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.05,
          "end": 15.63,
          "en": "Well, let's start with main.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.63,
          "end": 19.26,
          "en": "I can tell you that this is the main entry file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.26,
          "end": 20.82,
          "en": "of the entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.82,
          "end": 23.76,
          "en": "The code in this file is executed first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 27.57,
          "en": "when this website is being loaded in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.57,
          "end": 29.073,
          "en": "But what's this code doing?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30,
          "end": 35,
          "en": "Well, we're importing some things from React libraries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.91,
          "end": 39.51,
          "en": "This is, in the end, the modern JavaScript import syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.51,
          "end": 42.27,
          "en": "which is also supported by this React project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.27,
          "end": 43.65,
          "en": "we created here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.65,
          "end": 47.4,
          "en": "And we are importing some features from the React library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.4,
          "end": 50.313,
          "en": "and from the React DOM Library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.33,
          "end": 54.18,
          "en": "Now these libraries are installed in this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.18,
          "end": 56.91,
          "en": "with help of this package.json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.91,
          "end": 59.43,
          "en": "If you take a look at this package.json file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.43,
          "end": 63.78,
          "en": "under dependencies you find React and React DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.78,
          "end": 67.08,
          "en": "Now package.json is a file that's used by Node.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.08,
          "end": 69.81,
          "en": "for managing the dependencies of your project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.81,
          "end": 74.01,
          "en": "the third-party packages you want to use in your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.01,
          "end": 77.31,
          "en": "And it's also commonly used by front-end projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.31,
          "end": 80.67,
          "en": "where you don't build Node.js applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.67,
          "end": 84.45,
          "en": "for managing the packages of those projects as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.45,
          "end": 86.94,
          "en": "So therefore, this project, which we have here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.94,
          "end": 90.78,
          "en": "which I created with help of Vite but it would be the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.78,
          "end": 94.86,
          "en": "with Create React App, uses the package.json file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.86,
          "end": 99.03,
          "en": "to define external dependencies, to define which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.03,
          "end": 102.63,
          "en": "third-party packages will be used in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.63,
          "end": 105.3,
          "en": "And here we're using React and React DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.3,
          "end": 107.49000000000001,
          "en": "which are simply two separate libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.49000000000001,
          "end": 109.08,
          "en": "created by the same team.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.08,
          "end": 112.74000000000001,
          "en": "And these two libraries together form React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.74000000000001,
          "end": 115.25999999999999,
          "en": "the React Library you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.25999999999999,
          "end": 118.68,
          "en": "It's simply a combination of two packages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 123.48,
          "en": "Now in main.jsx, it all starts with this React DOM thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.48,
          "end": 126.753,
          "en": "because there we call the createRoot method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.83,
          "end": 132.83,
          "en": "This method takes a pointer at an element in our HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.07,
          "end": 138.45,
          "en": "And this is indeed regular, vanilla JavaScript code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.45,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "Document get element by ID is not React specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 145.89,
          "en": "And what this code does is it reaches out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.89,
          "end": 149.52,
          "en": "to this element here, which has the ID root",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.52,
          "end": 153.6,
          "en": "in this single HTML file that we have in this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 156.84300000000002,
          "en": "It's the only HTML file in the entire project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.74,
          "end": 162.51,
          "en": "So this code here, in main.jsx, reaches out to that root,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 162.51,
          "end": 167.28,
          "en": "to this DIV with ID root and then it calls the render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 167.28,
          "end": 172.28,
          "en": "method, in the end, on this object returned by createRoot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 172.38,
          "end": 174.99,
          "en": "It calls the render method, which is a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.99,
          "end": 179.46,
          "en": "provided by React, by that React DOM part of React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.46,
          "end": 181.41,
          "en": "to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.41,
          "end": 183.96,
          "en": "And we then do this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.96,
          "end": 188.25,
          "en": "We then pass some JSX code to render.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 188.25,
          "end": 193.25,
          "en": "And in the end this simply tells React that inside this DIV",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 194.34,
          "end": 198.93,
          "en": "with ID root, or in general the element with ID root,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 198.93,
          "end": 202.02,
          "en": "this React code should be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 202.02,
          "end": 204.84,
          "en": "So, should be displayed on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 204.84,
          "end": 208.82999999999998,
          "en": "Now this strict mode thing here is a special feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 208.82999999999998,
          "end": 212.79,
          "en": "offered by React, which is simply enabled some extra",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 212.79,
          "end": 217.07999999999998,
          "en": "checks warning us of potentially suboptimal code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 217.07999999999998,
          "end": 218.19,
          "en": "we could be writing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 218.19,
          "end": 221.64,
          "en": "Also in regards to future changes that might be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 221.64,
          "end": 225.36,
          "en": "by React where it wants to warn us if we write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 225.36,
          "end": 228.543,
          "en": "slightly outdated code or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 229.38,
          "end": 232.623,
          "en": "The more important part is this app thing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 233.46,
          "end": 237.75,
          "en": "because this is actually also being imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 237.75,
          "end": 242.73,
          "en": "This import, where we import app from ./app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 242.73,
          "end": 247.26,
          "en": "that in the end gives us an app thing, an app element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 247.26,
          "end": 250.32,
          "en": "as it seems, which is then rendered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 250.32,
          "end": 252.39,
          "en": "with help of this JSX feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 252.39,
          "end": 257.39,
          "en": "So, by using it like a HTML element in our JavaScript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 258.93,
          "end": 263.61,
          "en": "Now, ./app simply refers to the app.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 263.61,
          "end": 267.06,
          "en": "For JavaScript and JSX files you can and should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 267.06,
          "end": 270.36,
          "en": "omit the file extension here in your import statements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 270.36,
          "end": 273.51,
          "en": "and therefore this refers to app.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 273.51,
          "end": 278.493,
          "en": "And in there we are exporting a function called app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 279.72,
          "end": 281.94,
          "en": "That function is a very simple function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 281.94,
          "end": 286.94,
          "en": "All it does is it returns more JSX code, it returns the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 287.31,
          "end": 292.31,
          "en": "H1 HTML element with a text of \"Hello World\" inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 293.82,
          "end": 297.12,
          "en": "Now this is a so-called React component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 297.12,
          "end": 300.03,
          "en": "And React is all about components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 300.03,
          "end": 304.05,
          "en": "When you build React apps you, in the end, build components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 304.05,
          "end": 309.05,
          "en": "and components are simply functions that return JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 310.26,
          "end": 311.49,
          "en": "That's not entirely true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 311.49,
          "end": 314.55,
          "en": "Theoretically there are a few other things they could return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 314.55,
          "end": 318.42,
          "en": "as well, but typically they return JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 318.42,
          "end": 322.863,
          "en": "So functions that return JSX code are React components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 323.88,
          "end": 328.26,
          "en": "And React components can be used in other JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 328.26,
          "end": 332.07,
          "en": "That's why this app Function, as we just learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 332.07,
          "end": 335.58,
          "en": "which is imported in main.jsx, can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 335.58,
          "end": 339.39,
          "en": "like a HTML element in this JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 339.39,
          "end": 341.313,
          "en": "which is passed to render.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 342.21,
          "end": 346.05,
          "en": "Because render wants, in the end, some HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 346.05,
          "end": 349.59000000000003,
          "en": "some JSX code to be precise, that it should output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 349.59000000000003,
          "end": 352.89,
          "en": "on the screen, and we can use our own component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 352.89,
          "end": 356.163,
          "en": "the app component, as part of that JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 357.3,
          "end": 360.42,
          "en": "Now, our own component, the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 360.42,
          "end": 363.84,
          "en": "returns this H1 element, and therefore ultimately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 363.84,
          "end": 368.07,
          "en": "it's basically this H1 element which is passed to render,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 368.07,
          "end": 371.85,
          "en": "between those strict mode tags, which we can ignore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 371.85,
          "end": 375.15,
          "en": "And that's why we see \"Hello World\" on the screen here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 375.15,
          "end": 379.14300000000003,
          "en": "The content of this app component, which we have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 380.19,
          "end": 384.84,
          "en": "And I am aware that these are a couple of new concepts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 384.84,
          "end": 389.55,
          "en": "JSX components, definitely some new stuff here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 389.55,
          "end": 393.03,
          "en": "but they are also amongst the most important concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 393.03,
          "end": 395.43,
          "en": "React has to offer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 395.43,
          "end": 399.6,
          "en": "Because React is all about you writing your own components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 399.6,
          "end": 404.6,
          "en": "so your own functions that return HTML code in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 404.7,
          "end": 408.78,
          "en": "and using these different components for then composing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 408.78,
          "end": 411.9,
          "en": "a more complex user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 411.9,
          "end": 414.72,
          "en": "Because components are a key building block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 414.72,
          "end": 417.27,
          "en": "when working with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 417.27,
          "end": 422.22,
          "en": "Ultimately, any website you think of can be split up into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 422.22,
          "end": 425.7,
          "en": "different building blocks that make up the website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 425.7,
          "end": 430.68,
          "en": "like a header at the top, a sidebar on the left, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 430.68,
          "end": 433.53,
          "en": "And with React you simply build these",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 433.53,
          "end": 436.05,
          "en": "individual building blocks as functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 436.05,
          "end": 438.21,
          "en": "that return JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 438.21,
          "end": 440.85,
          "en": "And by combining these building blocks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 440.85,
          "end": 443.7,
          "en": "and potentially nesting them into each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 443.7,
          "end": 448.14,
          "en": "you can build complex user interfaces in a granular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 448.14,
          "end": 449.703,
          "en": "easy to manage way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 450.66,
          "end": 454.14,
          "en": "Now, it's not the only important feature added by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 454.14,
          "end": 456.45,
          "en": "but it's a key feature nonetheless,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 456.45,
          "end": 458.19,
          "en": "and they offer as a next step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 458.19,
          "end": 461.55,
          "en": "we'll start building our first custom component together,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 461.55,
          "end": 464.613,
          "en": "instead of just working with these predefined ones.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
